WEBVTT

00:29.112 --> 00:30.197
IN YOUR RADIANT SEASON

00:33.283 --> 00:34.909
CHARACTERS, EVENTS, ORGANIZATIONS,
AND PLACES IN THIS DRAMA ARE FICTITIOUS

00:34.910 --> 00:36.203
ALL CHILD ACTORS AND ANIMALS
FILMED IN A SAFE ENVIRONMENT

00:48.966 --> 00:49.967
What is it?

00:52.010 --> 00:53.053
Are you okay?

00:57.766 --> 01:00.309
Yes, it was just the lights.

01:00.310 --> 01:01.561
I'm fine.

01:02.688 --> 01:05.274
No, you don't look fine.

01:06.692 --> 01:07.775
I am.

01:07.776 --> 01:12.489
I won't cause you any trouble,
especially during the three-month trial.

01:17.953 --> 01:19.579
It was my first time
hearing that sound.

01:21.248 --> 01:25.751
It kind of sounded like tiny bits
of metal clinking or ice rattling.

01:25.752 --> 01:27.003
Right, the door!

01:27.004 --> 01:29.506
I think it came from outside the lab.

01:30.674 --> 01:31.757
EPISODE 4

01:31.758 --> 01:33.050
But I'm not sure what that sound was

01:33.051 --> 01:35.386
or why I was suddenly reminded
of the explosion.

01:36.930 --> 01:38.764
From everything I've heard so far,

01:38.765 --> 01:41.893
it's most likely
that it's a second trigger.

01:42.561 --> 01:44.229
A second trigger?

01:45.564 --> 01:46.689
It's nice to meet you.

01:46.690 --> 01:48.441
I'm Song Haran, the lead designer.

01:48.442 --> 01:52.278
It seems that
seeing her again acted as a trigger.

01:52.279 --> 01:55.323
She seems to have stimulated something,

01:55.324 --> 01:57.575
allowing you to remember
another piece of your past.

01:57.576 --> 02:00.244
Wait. No…

02:00.245 --> 02:02.955
That doesn't make any sense.

02:02.956 --> 02:05.082
I recalled everything seven years ago.

02:05.083 --> 02:09.086
When I first saw her at Jamsugyo,
I remembered everything in Boston.

02:09.087 --> 02:11.422
How are you sure it was everything?

02:11.423 --> 02:14.842
Well, because it was only
a temporary side effect

02:14.843 --> 02:17.970
from the shock of the accident.

02:17.971 --> 02:22.308
You're saying you remembered
everything at that moment?

02:22.309 --> 02:26.854
Yes. And I've never recalled
any new sounds or images since then.

02:26.855 --> 02:28.189
Not once.

02:28.190 --> 02:29.483
What if…

02:30.859 --> 02:32.861
Like this…

02:34.613 --> 02:38.700
What if there is still an empty spot
in your memories that you're not aware of?

02:39.618 --> 02:41.870
An empty spot?

02:42.454 --> 02:45.332
You seem like
a completely different person now.

02:45.916 --> 02:49.836
I can even picture
how hard you tried to change yourself.

02:51.254 --> 02:56.842
The harder you try to shake off the past,
the more your defense mechanisms kick in.

02:56.843 --> 02:59.595
Your unconscious mind
may overwrite painful memories

02:59.596 --> 03:02.808
to keep you from suffering any longer.

03:04.935 --> 03:09.481
It means there's still
an empty spot inside you.

03:11.983 --> 03:16.237
If that sound
is a part of that empty spot,

03:16.238 --> 03:18.448
is it a signal from the past

03:20.117 --> 03:23.495
telling me it's linked
to the explosion seven years ago?

03:26.832 --> 03:29.543
We can't be sure
of anything right now, but…

03:30.210 --> 03:31.877
it's certain that

03:31.878 --> 03:35.131
she's the one who has the key
to that empty spot inside you.

03:37.175 --> 03:39.177
You don't seem happy to see me.

03:39.845 --> 03:43.098
I mustered up my courage
to come and celebrate starting the trial.

03:47.352 --> 03:48.562
That's cold!

03:49.104 --> 03:53.567
Mmm. I always give a water show
to people I'm excited to see.

03:56.570 --> 03:58.238
Hey, look who it is!

03:58.822 --> 04:00.197
How have you been, Genius?

04:01.450 --> 04:04.994
-  How are you?
- It's been such a long time.

04:04.995 --> 04:06.579
What are you doing here so early?

04:06.580 --> 04:08.581
I wanted to have your coffee.

04:08.582 --> 04:10.541
I'm aching
from not having any for so long.

04:10.542 --> 04:12.710
Really? Then I should make you some now.

04:12.711 --> 04:13.836
Come on in.

04:13.837 --> 04:15.881
- Let's go, Genius.
-  Come inside.

04:18.216 --> 04:21.385
If you don't want to suffer again
because of your past,

04:21.386 --> 04:23.888
it would be best
to keep a distance from her.

04:23.889 --> 04:26.015
To protect yourself,

04:26.016 --> 04:29.227
a lock is safer than a key at the moment.

04:29.978 --> 04:31.855
A lock…

04:39.696 --> 04:41.989
- Sit down, roomie.
- Okay.

04:41.990 --> 04:44.825
Here's some coffee for my VVIP.

04:44.826 --> 04:46.536
Thank you.

04:46.912 --> 04:47.995
Huh?

04:47.996 --> 04:51.374
Right. It must have recovered
from the transplant shock.

04:52.167 --> 04:55.461
Good thing I repotted it, right?

04:56.713 --> 04:58.799
- Yes.
-  Right.

04:59.633 --> 05:01.218
It's a good thing you took it out.

05:04.095 --> 05:06.972
Even if I break down again,
I'll stay by her side.

05:06.973 --> 05:08.057
Mmm.

05:08.058 --> 05:11.352
She's the one
who gave me the life I have now.

05:11.353 --> 05:15.023
I would have died
if it hadn't been for her.

05:17.567 --> 05:18.693
Why are you staring at me?

05:19.528 --> 05:21.530
Mmm… Can't I look at you?

05:22.322 --> 05:24.407
Here. Cheers.

05:33.917 --> 05:35.669
Whatever's hiding in that empty spot,

05:36.628 --> 05:38.046
I'm going to deal with it.

05:38.797 --> 05:42.592
As long as she becomes happy,
I don't care what happens.

05:43.802 --> 05:45.178
I'll be careful

05:45.887 --> 05:49.182
so my existence doesn't reopen
her old wounds…

05:50.851 --> 05:53.353
and I'll do everything I can for her
before I leave again.

06:00.944 --> 06:02.863
IN YOUR RADIANT SEASON

06:05.156 --> 06:06.490
Did you check the data?

06:06.491 --> 06:07.741
Yes.

06:07.742 --> 06:10.786
The background team's research
was a little lacking.

06:10.787 --> 06:12.371
When did you organize all this?

06:12.372 --> 06:16.709
There was a lot of modernized material,
so I researched traditional hanok.

06:16.710 --> 06:20.754
I guess a Korean
should have researched traditional hanok.

06:21.840 --> 06:24.466
Okay,
I'll send this over to the EA team,

06:24.467 --> 06:27.761
and we can go down to Gyeongju on Tuesday.

06:27.762 --> 06:29.597
Oh. I'll join you a day late.

06:29.598 --> 06:33.100
Ms. Kim said she'll send over
the dancheong design draft on Tuesday.

06:33.101 --> 06:34.102
Mmm. Okay.

06:35.061 --> 06:37.396
But how will you get there, then?

06:37.397 --> 06:40.733
- I'll rent a car.
- Are you sure?

06:40.734 --> 06:43.778
I'll be absolutely fine.

06:48.575 --> 06:50.326
Hey, stop writing that.

06:50.327 --> 06:51.661
Fine.

06:52.245 --> 06:54.371
- Geez!
-  We'd like to pay.

06:54.372 --> 06:55.373
BEN IS AN IDIOT

06:56.541 --> 06:58.292
Ms. Song!

07:00.712 --> 07:02.130
What is he doing?

07:03.673 --> 07:04.758
You're done with work, right?

07:05.759 --> 07:07.093
Are you busy, by any chance?

07:07.552 --> 07:08.595
Nice!

07:09.971 --> 07:12.181
Then get in.

07:12.182 --> 07:16.143
- What? Where are we going?
- There's a car coming.

07:16.144 --> 07:21.231
I have a special lecture tomorrow,
so wrap up the contract with our buyer.

07:21.232 --> 07:22.859
- Yes, ma'am.
- Get in. Come on.

07:23.902 --> 07:25.819
Watch your head.

07:25.820 --> 07:26.821
Sorry!

07:28.156 --> 07:29.199
Oh, yeah.

07:30.325 --> 07:33.869
Did you just say, "Oh, yeah"?

07:33.870 --> 07:34.871
Those two.

07:35.747 --> 07:36.831
Keep an eye on them.

07:37.290 --> 07:38.291
Bye, then.

07:42.212 --> 07:43.963
So they weren't lying to me.

07:47.550 --> 07:49.718
We came all the way here for chicken?

07:49.719 --> 07:52.012
This is a must in Korea.

07:52.013 --> 07:54.391
Hangang River, picnic mat, and chicken.

07:55.141 --> 07:57.644
I'm also a tourist from abroad, you know.

07:58.395 --> 08:01.146
Wow!

08:01.147 --> 08:03.315
The Hangang River is so nice.

08:12.242 --> 08:14.119
I have something to give you. Sit down.

08:17.080 --> 08:19.790
There are 0.3, 0.4, 5, 6,

08:19.791 --> 08:22.543
oil-based, water-based,
nib tip, and ballpoint pens.

08:22.544 --> 08:25.254
Wait. Are you opening a stationery store?

08:25.255 --> 08:27.589
Who has this many pens?

08:27.590 --> 08:30.760
I have a habit of buying new pens
for people who lose their pens.

08:34.222 --> 08:36.850
There should at least be
one pen that you like.

08:42.605 --> 08:45.567
But the trial hasn't started yet.

08:46.234 --> 08:48.569
This is like a preview.

08:48.570 --> 08:49.820
A preview of what?

08:49.821 --> 08:53.240
I'll be away for about two weeks
starting Wednesday

08:53.241 --> 08:54.284
for a field survey.

08:55.118 --> 08:56.661
I said we'd get close,

08:57.328 --> 08:59.955
but if I left without doing anything,
nothing would change.

08:59.956 --> 09:01.082
And I didn't want that.

09:02.500 --> 09:04.251
So…

09:05.336 --> 09:06.463
will you take this, too?

09:08.506 --> 09:09.507
Oh…

09:10.258 --> 09:12.092
SEOUL DESTINATIONS LIST

09:12.093 --> 09:13.927
Why are you giving this to me?

09:13.928 --> 09:17.056
Choose where to go first
so we can go together later.

09:19.392 --> 09:21.686
The chicken's here.
I'll go get it.

09:22.520 --> 09:24.147
Can you clean that up?

09:25.273 --> 09:28.526
Oh. It's this way.
We have to eat chicken here, so hurry!

09:35.658 --> 09:36.868
"That person"?

09:39.829 --> 09:41.872
The night view is beautiful.

09:41.873 --> 09:42.956
Right?

09:42.957 --> 09:46.043
How about going to Jamsugyo on Christmas?
It's the best spot

09:46.044 --> 09:47.961
to watch the fireworks.

09:47.962 --> 09:49.756
-  I'd love that.
- Jamsugyo?

09:51.049 --> 09:52.133
Cheers.

10:01.976 --> 10:03.435
Goodness.

10:03.436 --> 10:04.937
We're really stuck.

10:04.938 --> 10:07.648
I heard they're showing fireworks
at 7:00.

10:07.649 --> 10:09.234
We're not moving at all.

10:12.195 --> 10:15.280
How long will it take?
I have an important meeting.

10:15.281 --> 10:18.451
If it's urgent, it would be faster
to just walk across the bridge.

10:21.830 --> 10:23.080
Mr. Yoon.

10:23.081 --> 10:24.999
The traffic's bad
since it's Christmas Eve.

10:26.292 --> 10:27.876
Really?

10:27.877 --> 10:29.837
Then take your time.

10:29.838 --> 10:31.131
All right.

11:12.338 --> 11:15.465
Hey, Kang Hyeokchan.
Why aren't you picking up?

11:15.466 --> 11:17.886
Sorry, I fell asleep.

11:18.845 --> 11:20.179
Maybe I have insomnia.

11:20.180 --> 11:23.765
My sleep pattern is messed up,
so I'm sleeping at random times.

11:23.766 --> 11:26.643
They said it helps with insomnia.

11:26.644 --> 11:28.855
Try listening to it
when you can't sleep. Okay?

11:35.904 --> 11:37.362
Let's go.

11:37.363 --> 11:39.072
- What? Right now?
- Yes.

11:39.073 --> 11:40.574
Should we order fried chicken?

11:40.575 --> 11:42.492
- Isn't seasoned chicken better?
- Hang on.

11:42.493 --> 11:43.994
No, fried is better.

11:43.995 --> 11:46.205
- Here you go!
-  What's this?

11:46.206 --> 11:47.706
You won some free chicken.

11:47.707 --> 11:49.875
- We can have this? Wow.
- Of course.

11:49.876 --> 11:51.585
It's still warm, so enjoy.

11:51.586 --> 11:53.420
Thank you.

11:54.714 --> 11:57.674
Come on. These are valuable,
so don't forget them.

11:59.677 --> 12:01.804
Chicken was too predictable, right?

12:02.472 --> 12:05.015
Let's go with charcoal-grilled meat.

12:05.016 --> 12:06.683
Ben recommended--

12:06.684 --> 12:08.978
All right, fine.

12:09.771 --> 12:10.896
But what's with these?

12:10.897 --> 12:12.398
Ah.

12:13.024 --> 12:16.444
We're going to cross Jamsugyo with these.
It's the fastest way.

12:17.528 --> 12:21.741
I'm sorry, but I'd like to just go now.

12:24.953 --> 12:26.536
No way.

12:26.537 --> 12:28.330
Can you not ride a bike?

12:28.331 --> 12:29.998
No, it's not that…

12:29.999 --> 12:32.000
No, it's okay.

12:32.001 --> 12:34.295
It's nothing to be ashamed of.

12:34.837 --> 12:36.922
- I'll return them.
- No, I…

12:36.923 --> 12:39.175
I know how to ride a bike, but…

12:41.761 --> 12:43.971
Fine. Let's go, then.

12:43.972 --> 12:44.973
Okay!

12:45.682 --> 12:46.766
All right.

12:47.392 --> 12:49.893
Since it's boring to just ride there,
how about a bet?

12:49.894 --> 12:52.521
The last one there buys dinner. Okay?

12:52.522 --> 12:54.147
No, there's no need…

12:54.148 --> 12:55.233
- Let's just--
- Ready, go!

12:57.110 --> 12:59.361
That's cheating.

13:05.410 --> 13:06.411
Oh…

13:07.203 --> 13:09.079
Whoa. Wait…

13:09.080 --> 13:11.248
Hang on! My leg…

13:11.249 --> 13:12.791
Wait, wait!

13:12.792 --> 13:14.585
What is it? What's wrong with your leg?

13:16.838 --> 13:17.839
It's long.

13:18.381 --> 13:19.464
What?

13:19.465 --> 13:20.966
Ah…

13:20.967 --> 13:22.802
Geez.

13:33.688 --> 13:34.689
Wow!

13:36.065 --> 13:37.066
Wow.

13:40.653 --> 13:41.654
Whoa.

14:12.435 --> 14:15.772
Wow, it's beautiful.

14:16.314 --> 14:17.315
Isn't it?

14:25.698 --> 14:28.159
Wow. The Hangang River is nice.

14:28.743 --> 14:31.119
Were you mimicking me?

14:31.120 --> 14:33.830
But that's not how you do it.

14:33.831 --> 14:37.209
Wow!

14:37.210 --> 14:39.461
Hangang River is really nice.

14:39.462 --> 14:40.545
What's the difference?

14:40.546 --> 14:42.005
- It sounds the same.
- It's different.

14:43.174 --> 14:44.759
I won, so you're buying.

14:47.095 --> 14:48.596
We haven't even gotten there yet.

14:55.353 --> 14:57.605
Good morning.

14:59.148 --> 15:00.690
Ah!

15:00.691 --> 15:02.777
-  Hi, Hadam.
-  Good morning.

15:04.237 --> 15:06.113
You know
Yougyum's coming today, right?

15:06.114 --> 15:07.989
He's coming at 7:00 p.m.,
so don't be late.

15:07.990 --> 15:10.992
Of course. We've been waiting
impatiently for this day.

15:10.993 --> 15:14.037
We'll have you rascals
sit down in front of us

15:14.038 --> 15:16.665
while we look him over from head to toe…

15:16.666 --> 15:19.543
Hey! I'm not done talking.

15:19.544 --> 15:21.045
You did go on for quite a bit.

15:23.214 --> 15:26.967
Haran, she can't be serious
about getting married, can she?

15:26.968 --> 15:30.138
I don't know. We'll see.

15:33.432 --> 15:36.643
CHEONGSOL BASEBALL TEAM CHA YOUGYUM
IS JOINING THE MAJOR LEAGUE

15:40.815 --> 15:42.190
No way. It's Han Sora.

15:42.191 --> 15:43.276
She came to school today?

15:44.110 --> 15:46.528
What? Who are you?

15:46.529 --> 15:47.946
Why do you want my number?

15:49.031 --> 15:52.784
Because I'm interested in you, of course.

15:54.370 --> 15:56.371
I'm not interested in you at all.

15:56.372 --> 15:57.831
And I have a girlfriend.

15:57.832 --> 15:59.249
Yougyum.

15:59.250 --> 16:00.334
Hey, Hadam.

16:03.963 --> 16:05.046
What's going on?

16:05.047 --> 16:06.423
It's nothing.

16:06.424 --> 16:09.218
Ah. Is she your girlfriend?

16:10.720 --> 16:12.138
I'll see you later.

16:17.935 --> 16:19.854
Who is she? Do you know her?

16:20.479 --> 16:23.732
Not at all.
It's the last time I'll even speak to her.

16:23.733 --> 16:25.442
Hey, don't you know? It's her.

16:25.443 --> 16:27.652
- Han Sora, the girl group trainee--
- Hadam!

16:27.653 --> 16:30.030
Have a good day. I'll see you later.

16:31.866 --> 16:33.992
- She must really like you.
-  Be quiet, will you?

16:33.993 --> 16:35.368
Come on!

16:35.369 --> 16:37.287
-  She's so pretty, though.
-  Right?

16:37.288 --> 16:38.496
Shut up, you guys.

16:38.497 --> 16:39.874
She has her eyes set on you.
You should date her.

16:40.416 --> 16:42.000
Be quiet. Shut up.

16:42.001 --> 16:44.003
That's the problem
with handsome guys.

16:44.879 --> 16:46.005
"Han Sora"?

17:04.732 --> 17:06.025
Hmm?

17:19.747 --> 17:21.748
This is Design Team 1 of Nana Atelier--

17:21.749 --> 17:23.334
Why isn't anyone picking up?

17:25.962 --> 17:27.212
Why are you calling here?

17:27.213 --> 17:28.923
This is urgent. Listen carefully.

17:29.048 --> 17:31.884
It's a womenswear lecture,
but I brought menswear materials.

17:32.009 --> 17:35.387
- That's on me. We don't have much time.
- Taxi! Taxi! Over here!

17:35.388 --> 17:37.597
I need you here in 30 minutes.

17:37.598 --> 17:40.101
What do I do?

17:44.772 --> 17:47.440
- Hey, my neighbor!
- Oh… Do you have some time?

17:47.441 --> 17:49.401
Sure, I'm totally free.

17:49.402 --> 17:51.111
I rented this car, so I'm taking a drive--

17:51.112 --> 17:53.029
That's great! Then…

17:53.030 --> 17:55.031
Then can you…

17:55.032 --> 17:57.450
I have an urgent meeting,
but I can't get a cab.

17:57.451 --> 17:59.619
It's a 15-minute drive.
Please give me a ride.

17:59.620 --> 18:01.746
Well, I…

18:01.747 --> 18:03.540
But I…

18:03.541 --> 18:04.709
Yeah?

18:05.710 --> 18:07.545
All right.

18:17.805 --> 18:20.557
Do you know you're driving
20 km an hour right now?

18:20.558 --> 18:22.559
You can drive up to 60 here.

18:22.560 --> 18:26.272
I'm sorry, but can't you go a bit faster?
I only have 20 minutes left.

18:27.898 --> 18:29.400
Okay.

18:34.905 --> 18:36.824
Watch out!

18:46.125 --> 18:47.501
Hey!

18:47.627 --> 18:49.420
Hey, get out.

18:50.755 --> 18:52.797
Get out of the car.

18:57.511 --> 18:59.888
I almost got hit because of you.

18:59.889 --> 19:02.099
You can't just cut in like that.

19:02.642 --> 19:06.270
I'm sorry. I'll take care of any damages.

19:06.854 --> 19:07.855
Uh…

19:09.023 --> 19:11.399
Okay. I'll pick it up right away.

19:11.400 --> 19:12.777
I'm so sorry.

19:28.626 --> 19:30.961
Ms. Song, look at me.

19:32.630 --> 19:34.130
I'm sorry about that.

19:34.131 --> 19:35.465
But everything's fine.

19:35.466 --> 19:38.093
I took care of everything. It's fine.

19:38.094 --> 19:40.553
Are you okay?
Are you sure you're not hurt?

19:40.554 --> 19:44.183
I shouldn't have
asked you for a ride.

19:45.059 --> 19:47.603
Nothing happened,
and no one's hurt. It's fine.

19:51.440 --> 19:52.858
MS. KIM

19:53.609 --> 19:56.487
I'm sorry, but I don't think
I can take you. Uh…

19:57.530 --> 20:00.990
There's a cab over there.
You're in a hurry, so go.

20:00.991 --> 20:04.202
I'll take care of everything here,
so don't worry.

20:07.289 --> 20:10.000
Getting close to someone
is really difficult…

20:10.584 --> 20:12.920
No, it's scary for me.

20:14.004 --> 20:16.132
If no one is special to me,

20:17.174 --> 20:19.468
then at least nothing bad will happen.

20:38.904 --> 20:39.989
Earlier…

20:44.910 --> 20:48.329
I'm sorry about what happened earlier.

20:48.330 --> 20:52.084
No, I'm sorry.
I shouldn't have forced you like that.

20:54.170 --> 20:55.755
It was because of your ear, right?

20:57.173 --> 20:59.174
It seemed that way.

21:05.723 --> 21:09.601
A few years ago,
Ben got injured because of me.

21:09.602 --> 21:11.729
There was a honk on my left side,

21:12.938 --> 21:14.523
but I couldn't react properly,

21:15.399 --> 21:16.484
like earlier.

21:18.527 --> 21:23.115
Since then, I told myself
I would never give anyone a ride,

21:24.200 --> 21:25.617
but…

21:25.618 --> 21:29.413
Today was the first time,
so I guess I was anxious.

21:30.831 --> 21:32.123
I'm sorry.

21:32.124 --> 21:33.542
You're scared

21:34.627 --> 21:35.878
of bad things happening,

21:36.545 --> 21:37.963
but I made you go through that.

21:42.426 --> 21:45.721
Your free trial
is proving to be effective, though.

21:47.681 --> 21:51.435
Back at the Hangang River,
and in the car earlier,

21:52.019 --> 21:53.478
it helped me a lot.

21:58.150 --> 22:01.821
I don't exactly have good memories
about Jamsugyo.

22:05.032 --> 22:08.201
I thought I'd only have sad memories
about it forever,

22:08.202 --> 22:09.662
but I realized I could smile there.

22:10.287 --> 22:15.251
Perhaps I can overwrite
those sad memories, too.

22:16.502 --> 22:18.087
I thought that for the first time.

22:19.171 --> 22:23.676
And I was really scared back in the car,
but I recovered quickly thanks to you.

22:25.386 --> 22:28.806
If it were a few days ago,
I would have just tried to flee again.

22:30.182 --> 22:31.308
But I won't now.

22:33.143 --> 22:35.645
At least until the trial is over,

22:35.646 --> 22:37.273
I won't enter my cave again.

22:38.816 --> 22:42.319
So don't blame yourself, okay?

22:48.576 --> 22:50.953
I'm relieved.

22:52.913 --> 22:53.998
To be honest,

22:55.332 --> 22:57.084
I was pretty scared.

22:58.878 --> 23:00.588
You just mustered up your courage,

23:01.922 --> 23:03.966
and I was worried you'd run away again.

23:05.175 --> 23:07.052
I said we'd have fun,

23:07.720 --> 23:11.307
but I thought I'd already ruined it.

23:13.601 --> 23:15.143
Keep teaching me.

23:15.144 --> 23:17.187
I'll do my best to learn.

23:23.694 --> 23:25.028
I'll get going now. Bye.

23:25.029 --> 23:26.571
Okay. Bye.

23:28.699 --> 23:29.866
Ah.

23:29.867 --> 23:31.243
I actually don't like…

23:32.620 --> 23:34.914
everything being okay and only having fun.

23:35.497 --> 23:37.249
That's fake friendship.

23:38.584 --> 23:40.919
Being able to tell each other
when you're not okay

23:40.920 --> 23:42.129
is real friendship, right?

23:44.840 --> 23:47.759
So let's tell each other in advance
if something's wrong

23:47.760 --> 23:49.845
so we won't have to feel guilty
like today.

23:50.804 --> 23:53.348
All right.

23:53.349 --> 23:56.100
But you should stop that
if you want real friendship.

23:56.101 --> 23:57.353
Stop what?

23:59.396 --> 24:02.358
You don't have to worry so much
about my hearing.

24:02.900 --> 24:04.192
What? Me?

24:05.444 --> 24:09.239
- I wasn't worried about that at all.
-  It's pretty obvious, you know.

24:09.823 --> 24:13.786
Ever since you found out,
you've been standing to my right.

24:14.662 --> 24:19.123
I'm usually fine,
so you don't have to do that, okay?

24:19.124 --> 24:24.088
Well, it's been a long time
since I made a new friend,

24:24.755 --> 24:28.716
so I'm not really sure what I have to do.

24:28.717 --> 24:29.969
You seem mature,

24:31.095 --> 24:32.428
but you're a picky eater.

24:32.429 --> 24:34.807
You love Mr. Park's coffee,

24:35.391 --> 24:37.685
you ride a bike very well,

24:38.602 --> 24:41.313
and you pretend not to be,
but you're pretty caring.

24:42.314 --> 24:43.398
What?

24:43.399 --> 24:45.025
This is how you become friends.

24:46.318 --> 24:48.319
Slowly, without forcing anything,

24:48.320 --> 24:50.781
by finding out small things
about each other.

24:53.033 --> 24:56.035
I also don't like oysters.
They're like snot.

24:56.036 --> 24:58.037
What? Snot?

24:58.038 --> 24:59.707
I just told you more about myself.

25:01.625 --> 25:04.003
Is this not how you do it?

25:05.504 --> 25:06.879
It is. That's right.

25:06.880 --> 25:08.757
Give me your hand. I'll give you a stamp.

25:10.092 --> 25:11.927
Here. A "great job" stamp.

25:15.139 --> 25:18.058
I told you a secret,
so next time it's your turn.

25:20.978 --> 25:24.773
It doesn't have to be anything big.
Just a small one.

25:26.316 --> 25:27.317
Bye, then.

25:29.903 --> 25:30.988
Bye.

25:36.827 --> 25:37.828
A secret…

25:46.170 --> 25:48.212
Hmm. Hair, check.

25:48.213 --> 25:51.340
Your outfit's nice…
and your face is even nicer.

25:51.341 --> 25:54.010
You're perfect.

25:54.011 --> 25:55.636
I'm so nervous.

25:55.637 --> 25:58.222
I wasn't even this nervous
at the Comets press conference.

25:58.223 --> 26:00.725
It's okay to be nervous.

26:00.726 --> 26:02.101
Just be yourself.

26:02.102 --> 26:06.022
Wow. Hearing you say that
suddenly made me calm.

26:06.023 --> 26:08.817
Then hold my hand.

26:13.322 --> 26:16.366
I'm actually really nervous.

26:17.701 --> 26:19.912
Just trust me. Let's do this.

26:20.746 --> 26:22.331
Okay.

26:24.583 --> 26:26.167
You're finally here.

26:26.168 --> 26:28.337
Let's see who this guy is.

26:29.254 --> 26:31.173
Hello. I'm Cha Yougyum.

26:36.678 --> 26:38.639
It's a green light!

26:54.071 --> 26:56.739
Why did you get here late?

26:56.740 --> 26:58.367
Who did you help?

26:59.201 --> 27:00.202
An elderly woman.

27:00.911 --> 27:04.539
She was standing in the middle
of the crosswalk at a red light.

27:04.540 --> 27:05.915
It looked dangerous.

27:05.916 --> 27:08.544
Are you all right, ma'am?
Where are you headed?

27:09.753 --> 27:12.256
It seemed like she might have dementia.

27:13.799 --> 27:15.008
Oh…

27:24.726 --> 27:27.271
It's nice to meet you.

27:27.771 --> 27:30.524
Hadam doesn't know,
so pretend you never saw me.

27:35.070 --> 27:36.530
Isn't he handsome?

27:39.324 --> 27:41.785
What? Yougyum, are you crying?

27:42.369 --> 27:44.370
Huh?

27:44.371 --> 27:46.330
Oh, I…

27:46.331 --> 27:49.459
I'm just so happy
to meet your grandmother.

27:50.711 --> 27:52.044
I couldn't help it.

28:11.899 --> 28:13.901
Why aren't they picking up?

28:22.993 --> 28:26.079
My sisters aren't picking up.
We should just…

28:28.165 --> 28:29.833
Why are you sweating?

28:31.001 --> 28:32.920
- Is it hot?
- Oh.

28:34.504 --> 28:36.089
I'm not feeling so well.

28:37.925 --> 28:39.926
I'll come back when her sisters are here.

28:39.927 --> 28:41.303
- What?
- Will you?

28:42.304 --> 28:43.721
I'll see you again next time.

28:43.722 --> 28:44.806
See you at school.

28:47.893 --> 28:48.894
Yougyum!

28:52.856 --> 28:54.357
What was that, Grandma?

28:54.358 --> 28:57.526
You didn't even look at him
and didn't say a word.

28:57.527 --> 28:59.654
He left because
you made him uncomfortable.

28:59.655 --> 29:00.905
Hadam.

29:00.906 --> 29:02.990
I'm not feeling well today, either--

29:02.991 --> 29:04.742
Haran and Hayeong didn't even come.

29:04.743 --> 29:06.994
He's really important to me.
How can you do this?

29:06.995 --> 29:09.580
Did you think I was joking
about getting married?

29:09.581 --> 29:11.374
- Hadam.
- I can't believe this!

29:12.918 --> 29:14.711
- Yougyum!
- Hadam!

29:19.174 --> 29:21.927
How could he be…

29:31.478 --> 29:32.561
Hayeong!

29:32.562 --> 29:35.147
- Why are you so late?
- Well, I…

29:35.148 --> 29:36.691
- There's chalk on your face.
- Yougyum!

29:37.776 --> 29:38.777
Hadam!

29:39.653 --> 29:40.654
Did Yougyum leave?

29:41.863 --> 29:45.199
I'm sorry, things were hectic.
I didn't notice the time.

29:45.200 --> 29:46.617
I'm really sorry, too.

29:46.618 --> 29:48.577
We have a fitting tomorrow,
but the sample--

29:48.578 --> 29:50.705
Right. Sure.

29:50.706 --> 29:52.457
I'm sure you had your reasons.

29:53.250 --> 29:54.333
It's fine.

29:54.334 --> 29:56.502
You're so generous.

29:56.503 --> 29:57.962
You have a big heart…

29:57.963 --> 29:59.880
Or maybe not.

29:59.881 --> 30:02.341
You're not okay, are you?

30:02.342 --> 30:03.926
You're angry, right?

30:03.927 --> 30:05.512
Yes. Very.

30:06.638 --> 30:09.933
I'm holding back my anger,
so don't talk to me.

30:16.815 --> 30:21.110
Are you jealous because I'm doing
way better than you?

30:21.111 --> 30:22.237
You're so annoying!

30:29.828 --> 30:31.663
Oh, no…

30:37.127 --> 30:39.588
Grandma, why did Yougyum leave so quickly?

30:40.172 --> 30:42.716
Um… He must not be feeling well.

30:43.633 --> 30:46.011
I should go shower. Go upstairs.

30:47.846 --> 30:49.096
What?

30:49.097 --> 30:52.391
Doesn't Grandma seem like she's unwell?

30:52.392 --> 30:54.352
Maybe the lecture was pretty tough.

31:39.898 --> 31:42.317
Are you all right, ma'am?
Where are you headed?

31:43.902 --> 31:46.613
I'm not sure.

31:47.197 --> 31:50.158
I can't remember where I was going.

31:54.871 --> 31:57.874
It's okay. We'll cross the street together
when it's a green light.

32:24.109 --> 32:25.568
Hadam. I'm sorry.

32:25.569 --> 32:27.821
Tell Yougyum to come back next time, okay?

33:13.700 --> 33:14.701
Yes, Mr. Cha.

33:15.327 --> 33:16.493
Lunch?

33:16.494 --> 33:18.787
I'd love that. I'll head there now.

33:18.788 --> 33:21.165
- Okay.
- Ms. Song.

33:21.166 --> 33:22.209
Yes?

33:28.798 --> 33:30.090
Ms. Kim is asking for you.

33:30.091 --> 33:31.426
Me?

33:34.179 --> 33:38.182
Wait. I went there last time,
but she'd already gone home.

33:38.183 --> 33:40.893
Why do you keep playing pranks?
It doesn't suit you.

33:40.894 --> 33:43.479
I mixed up the date.
She wanted to see you today.

33:43.480 --> 33:45.940
You should go see her now.

33:45.941 --> 33:47.107
You mean it?

33:48.401 --> 33:51.363
All right, then.

33:54.574 --> 33:56.408
Yes, Mr. Cha.

33:56.409 --> 33:59.913
I don't think I can go. I'm sorry.

34:00.830 --> 34:03.457
I don't know. She keeps asking for me.

34:03.458 --> 34:04.834
MEN'S HEALTH
SEONGWON BRANCH

34:13.468 --> 34:15.595
Just a minute.

34:16.179 --> 34:17.388
Come in.

34:17.389 --> 34:19.431
Ms. Kim.

34:19.432 --> 34:21.517
I heard you asked for me.

34:21.518 --> 34:23.520
Were you dreaming? I didn't ask for you.

34:24.062 --> 34:26.438
- Get out. Don't bother me.
- Eh?

34:26.439 --> 34:29.984
What's with Mr. Yeon?
Why does he keep lying to me?

34:29.985 --> 34:31.860
I'd like you to talk to yourself outside.

34:31.861 --> 34:33.071
Okay.

34:33.655 --> 34:35.115
I'll excuse myself, then.

34:39.869 --> 34:41.204
Did I ask for her?

34:42.163 --> 34:43.164
I don't think I did.

35:05.895 --> 35:08.480
Sol, the shoulder is 17 inches, right?

35:08.481 --> 35:10.900
-  Oh. One moment, please.
-  Okay.

35:12.027 --> 35:14.070
What's going on? Something's off.

35:15.113 --> 35:17.531
Something's different from usual.

35:17.532 --> 35:19.534
What? What's different?

35:20.493 --> 35:21.494
What?

35:26.207 --> 35:27.333
Right. It's that.

35:27.334 --> 35:29.543
She hasn't pushed the button once today.

35:30.795 --> 35:32.255
You're right!

35:43.058 --> 35:44.683
-  Are you okay?
-  I'm sorry.

35:45.977 --> 35:47.269
Two, four…

35:47.270 --> 35:49.272
Look at the time.

35:49.939 --> 35:51.983
What a surprise.

35:53.276 --> 35:54.735
What? Gyeongju?

35:54.736 --> 35:56.403
The costume team, too?

35:56.404 --> 35:58.739
Yes, it was our director's idea.

35:58.740 --> 36:00.616
He said a better understanding
of the background

36:00.617 --> 36:02.785
would help with the costumes.

36:02.786 --> 36:03.953
Right.

36:04.663 --> 36:07.666
We won't be able to capture the details
with the script alone.

36:08.416 --> 36:09.417
Then shall we…

36:13.254 --> 36:14.338
Ah.

36:14.339 --> 36:16.882
My schedule's packed,

36:16.883 --> 36:19.927
so you can go as long as
it doesn't interfere with other work.

36:19.928 --> 36:21.970
I'm ready to go!

36:21.971 --> 36:25.099
I've been buried in fabric dust.
I'll finally get some fresh air!

36:25.100 --> 36:28.103
You're not going on a picnic.
Get fresh air on your day off.

36:29.312 --> 36:31.605
You know I'll work hard there.

36:31.606 --> 36:32.940
Picnic, beep.

36:32.941 --> 36:36.652
Business trip, ding ding ding.

36:36.653 --> 36:39.614
I think two nights will be enough
for your team. Is that okay?

36:40.115 --> 36:43.784
Then our costume team
will head there on Thursday.

36:43.785 --> 36:44.869
All right.

37:06.599 --> 37:07.892
Hey, Yang Changmo!

37:08.935 --> 37:10.103
Hey, Hadam.

37:11.896 --> 37:13.063
Where's Yougyum?

37:13.064 --> 37:14.565
He said he had to go somewhere.

37:14.566 --> 37:17.861
Oh… Wasn't he meeting up with you?

37:18.862 --> 37:19.863
Huh?

37:23.032 --> 37:24.908
How are we going to get through today?

37:24.909 --> 37:26.201
We do it every day.

37:26.202 --> 37:27.411
Yougyum!

37:27.412 --> 37:28.579
Hey.

37:28.580 --> 37:29.831
Go ahead.

37:31.040 --> 37:32.292
Sorry about yesterday.

37:32.959 --> 37:34.668
Let's talk after your practice.

37:34.669 --> 37:38.339
No, I'm sorry.
I didn't take care of myself properly.

37:39.466 --> 37:43.051
But sorry, Changmo asked to see me later.

37:43.052 --> 37:47.015
Maybe he needs my advice
on something.

37:50.727 --> 37:52.687
Yougyum, what are you doing?

37:53.980 --> 37:55.774
You said you're meeting Changmo.

37:56.649 --> 37:57.858
Did you meet him?

37:57.859 --> 37:59.903
What? Yes, why?

38:00.403 --> 38:02.321
- Is something up?
- Huh?

38:03.406 --> 38:05.325
No, I was just calling.

38:06.326 --> 38:07.702
Bye, then.

38:25.094 --> 38:26.095
Oh?

38:26.679 --> 38:28.138
Yougyum…

38:28.139 --> 38:29.349
Yougyum!

38:40.902 --> 38:42.195
I'll see you later.

38:49.702 --> 38:51.370
I wanted to meet you, too.

38:51.371 --> 38:53.081
Are you happy? Enjoying your date?

38:54.165 --> 38:56.625
- Hadam!
- How could you meet Han Sora--

38:56.626 --> 38:57.669
Hadam.

39:00.547 --> 39:03.258
- What are you doing here?
- I'm here too.

39:06.219 --> 39:09.179
What? You were waiting
in front of our school?

39:09.180 --> 39:10.639
You didn't even know his face.

39:10.640 --> 39:14.142
How could we not know him?
He was even on the news.

39:16.145 --> 39:17.438
They threatened you, didn't they?

39:18.022 --> 39:20.649
That's why you lied to me, right?

39:20.650 --> 39:24.278
I told him not to tell you
because we wanted to apologize.

39:24.279 --> 39:26.154
No, there's no need.

39:26.155 --> 39:28.324
I left early
because I wasn't feeling well.

39:29.367 --> 39:33.579
But who's Han Sora?
You said something about Han Sora.

39:33.580 --> 39:38.041
I don't know what you're talking about.

39:38.042 --> 39:40.336
Let's eat.

39:44.173 --> 39:46.425
Mmm. This is good.

39:48.344 --> 39:49.387
Hey, Hadam.

39:49.929 --> 39:52.015
-  You said you're meeting Changmo.
- Huh?

39:52.599 --> 39:53.891
Did you meet him?

39:53.892 --> 39:56.602
What? Yes, why? Is something up?

39:56.603 --> 39:59.230
Huh? No, I was just calling.

39:59.898 --> 40:01.649
Okay.

40:06.988 --> 40:08.698
There's a visitor? Who…

40:14.787 --> 40:17.372
Is it pretty bad?

40:17.373 --> 40:19.833
My mind goes blank
from time to time.

40:19.834 --> 40:22.670
I sometimes buy the same book
two or three times.

40:24.213 --> 40:28.259
I'm usually fine,
but there are days I'm not,

40:30.428 --> 40:31.930
like the day I met you.

40:33.181 --> 40:35.558
Uh… Did you see a doctor?

40:37.268 --> 40:40.855
I got a basic checkup,
and they said there were signs.

40:41.439 --> 40:44.776
I scheduled a follow-up exam
in a few weeks.

40:46.903 --> 40:48.738
But at my age,

40:50.406 --> 40:52.241
you can sense it.

40:52.992 --> 40:55.452
It's probably right.

40:58.706 --> 41:02.209
I'm not sure what to do.

41:02.210 --> 41:04.044
You should tell your family--

41:04.045 --> 41:05.212
No.

41:05.213 --> 41:07.548
I have to focus on what I can do now.

41:08.967 --> 41:12.803
I don't know how much longer
I'll be myself.

41:12.804 --> 41:16.224
I have to take care of things
and receive treatment while I can.

41:19.477 --> 41:23.022
I'm sorry to burden you,
but please do me a favor.

41:23.982 --> 41:25.315
The fries here are good.

41:25.316 --> 41:27.150
Hadam, try this.
You like these, right?

41:27.151 --> 41:31.531
Haran has already lost
many loved ones.

41:32.156 --> 41:33.992
I don't want to be a burden to her now.

41:34.826 --> 41:37.661
Hayeong is always so loud
and quick to laugh.

41:37.662 --> 41:41.124
But if she finds out about my condition,
she won't be able to smile again.

41:42.834 --> 41:44.210
Hadam's in her senior year.

41:44.711 --> 41:48.172
She needs to focus on her studies.
I won't be the reason she falls apart.

41:48.965 --> 41:50.383
So please...

41:51.843 --> 41:52.844
For now,

41:53.469 --> 41:55.555
keep this a secret.

42:03.771 --> 42:05.773
I don't have much time.

42:11.863 --> 42:14.657
How badly did they scrape it?

42:15.491 --> 42:18.493
Are you the one who called me
about the accident?

42:23.583 --> 42:26.501
I did call you, but there was no accident.

42:26.502 --> 42:29.172
What… Then why would you say
there was an accident?

42:30.256 --> 42:31.757
Hang on.

42:31.758 --> 42:32.966
It's you, isn't it?

42:32.967 --> 42:34.969
- I have it all planned out.
- Mr. Cha Min?

42:37.472 --> 42:39.598
I'll treat you to something nice.

42:55.573 --> 42:57.575
What was that? What's with him?

42:58.367 --> 43:01.036
The guy in the hotel parking lot
who reversed into me.

43:01.037 --> 43:02.412
Who are you--

43:02.413 --> 43:03.915
That's not your business.

43:04.999 --> 43:09.127
Why don't you sort out
all the women you've been juggling?

43:09.128 --> 43:12.297
What are you saying?
Who are you to order me around?

43:12.298 --> 43:15.258
It would be best
to say you got transferred abroad

43:15.259 --> 43:16.718
so no one feels hurt.

43:16.719 --> 43:19.639
If you don't stop acting like a scumbag,

43:21.349 --> 43:23.476
we'll be meeting again.

43:26.437 --> 43:27.730
Hey!

43:30.066 --> 43:32.442
That's what you call being a scumbag.

43:32.443 --> 43:34.736
Do you want the other one broken, too?

43:34.737 --> 43:37.448
Whether you break it or not,
just sort out your women problem.

43:38.032 --> 43:40.867
I suggest sending out DMs right now.

43:40.868 --> 43:44.746
Mmm…  No, thanks.

43:44.747 --> 43:46.957
I'm not going to.

43:46.958 --> 43:49.584
It's all because I'm popular.

43:49.585 --> 43:51.461
What are you going to do?

43:51.462 --> 43:52.546
Oh…

43:52.547 --> 43:54.215
Wait. Hey. Hey!

43:54.966 --> 43:56.551
My phone.

43:58.719 --> 43:59.720
Hey!

44:01.180 --> 44:02.681
If you don't sort them out,

44:02.682 --> 44:04.517
the next thing you'll lose…

44:06.477 --> 44:08.187
won't be your phone.

44:15.236 --> 44:16.319
Wait.

44:16.320 --> 44:17.697
- Hang on.
- Hello.

44:18.489 --> 44:20.783
I want to schedule a car repair.

44:21.367 --> 44:22.617
My phone's in there.

44:22.618 --> 44:24.661
What are you doing?

44:24.662 --> 44:26.914
I'm heading out!

44:29.917 --> 44:31.918
- Whoa. Oh…
- I'll drive.

44:31.919 --> 44:33.753
What are you doing here?

44:33.754 --> 44:35.297
We're going to Gyeongju.

44:35.298 --> 44:37.424
I'm going to Gyeongju,
but the costume team--

44:37.425 --> 44:38.717
I'm going today, too.

44:38.718 --> 44:40.635
Can you load my luggage?

44:40.636 --> 44:41.720
Oh…

44:43.598 --> 44:44.599
Sure…

44:47.768 --> 44:48.769
Mmm…

44:50.021 --> 44:52.355
Wow. I feel pretty happy.

44:52.356 --> 44:54.567
You're worried about me.

44:55.276 --> 44:56.818
Worried?

44:56.819 --> 44:57.820
Me?

44:58.529 --> 45:02.824
You were worried about
me driving after what happened last time.

45:02.825 --> 45:04.202
When did I…

45:07.038 --> 45:08.872
You're right.

45:08.873 --> 45:11.500
It must be your first time
driving on a highway in Korea.

45:13.002 --> 45:14.086
Thanks.

45:19.258 --> 45:21.927
But do you usually do
field research for animations?

45:21.928 --> 45:22.970
Of course.

45:23.596 --> 45:25.972
You know Arendelle, right?

45:25.973 --> 45:29.768
That was based on
a lakeside town called Hallstatt.

45:29.769 --> 45:36.734
And the ice castle was inspired
by a hotel built of ice in Quebec.

45:37.318 --> 45:39.277
And Won is Korean,

45:39.278 --> 45:41.530
so we're looking
for her background in Korea.

45:42.073 --> 45:44.908
We have to decide
where she grew up and how

45:44.909 --> 45:47.369
so we can blend that into the story.

45:47.370 --> 45:51.498
You had the vibe of a local bum,
but you seem like a pro now.

45:51.499 --> 45:52.707
A local bum?

45:52.708 --> 45:54.209
Geez.

45:54.210 --> 45:57.545
I didn't want to say this myself,
but I'll just say it.

45:57.546 --> 45:59.631
I'm pretty competent.

45:59.632 --> 46:01.466
I get lots of job offers, too.

46:01.467 --> 46:02.884
I meant it's nice

46:02.885 --> 46:05.471
seeing you look so excited
talking about work.

46:08.975 --> 46:10.058
Hang on.

46:11.727 --> 46:12.728
Hey, Ben.

46:13.896 --> 46:15.146
Well, we're…

46:15.147 --> 46:16.649
We're almost halfway there.

46:17.483 --> 46:18.776
We're almost halfway there.

46:19.360 --> 46:21.862
Oh. I'm going with Ms. Song.

46:22.989 --> 46:24.322
It just happened.

46:24.323 --> 46:25.448
See you later.

46:29.704 --> 46:31.831
I can smell rain.

46:45.011 --> 46:46.554
Is it a shower?

46:47.847 --> 46:48.848
Mmm.

46:49.348 --> 46:52.851
But I heard it's the smell
of organic matter diffusing,

46:52.852 --> 46:54.394
not the rain.

46:54.395 --> 46:56.521
- What was it again?
- Petrichor.

46:56.522 --> 46:57.606
Right, petrichor.

46:58.691 --> 47:00.358
You're really good at this stuff.

47:00.359 --> 47:03.279
You said something about hypochlorite
at the police station, too.

47:04.113 --> 47:06.365
It seems like you majored
in engineering, not art.

47:12.747 --> 47:15.457
Oh? It stopped. What's going on?

47:15.458 --> 47:16.624
Huh?

47:16.625 --> 47:17.752
Is it not working?

47:18.252 --> 47:20.128
No. Didn't they check this car?

47:20.129 --> 47:21.756
I got it checked.

47:23.132 --> 47:25.675
It's not raining much yet, though.

47:28.095 --> 47:29.262
What…

47:29.263 --> 47:31.389
Wait. It's raining too much.

47:31.390 --> 47:32.932
Just pull over to the side.

47:32.933 --> 47:34.225
Pull over?

47:36.729 --> 47:38.104
UNDER CONSTRUCTION
NO SHOULDER AHEAD

47:38.105 --> 47:40.523
Huh? "No shoulder ahead"?

47:40.524 --> 47:41.941
Then what do we do?

47:41.942 --> 47:43.902
It's not like we can make a road.

47:43.903 --> 47:45.987
- First…
- Check if there are any cars.

47:45.988 --> 47:47.655
Hang on. I'll take care of it.

47:48.824 --> 47:50.867
Oh no. I can't see anything. What do I do?

47:50.868 --> 47:52.787
Wait.

47:53.788 --> 47:55.498
- Hang on.
- I can't see anything.

47:58.626 --> 48:00.668
- What are you doing?
- This won't work.

48:00.669 --> 48:02.462
Check if there are any cars coming!

48:02.463 --> 48:03.588
I can't see anything.

48:03.589 --> 48:05.006
SOMUNGYEONG REST STOP

48:05.007 --> 48:06.883
- It's a rest stop!
- A rest stop?

48:06.884 --> 48:08.468
I can't see the road, though.

48:08.469 --> 48:12.847
I'll keep my eye on the road,
so keep driving.

48:12.848 --> 48:13.932
But I can't see.

48:13.933 --> 48:15.809
I'll count to three,

48:15.810 --> 48:18.478
- so turn right when I get to three.
- Okay.

48:18.479 --> 48:19.562
All right…

48:19.563 --> 48:21.607
One, two,

48:22.525 --> 48:23.608
three.

48:28.364 --> 48:31.367
SOMUNGYEONG REST STOP

48:50.928 --> 48:52.095
Ah…

48:52.096 --> 48:53.805
Take a breather.

48:53.806 --> 48:55.766
I'll call the rental shop.

48:56.392 --> 48:57.601
Oh…

49:03.691 --> 49:05.818
What? Four to five hours?

49:07.194 --> 49:08.570
The motor's completely out.

49:08.571 --> 49:09.904
We can't fix it here.

49:09.905 --> 49:12.073
I'll take it to a repair shop nearby.

49:12.074 --> 49:15.494
If you want a replacement,
we'll send you another car tomorrow.

49:16.078 --> 49:17.121
I'm sorry.

49:25.337 --> 49:27.756
Yes, we probably won't get there
until tonight.

49:29.091 --> 49:31.760
Okay, Ben. I'll call you again
when we're heading out.

49:32.386 --> 49:33.471
Okay.

49:40.895 --> 49:42.353
Here, wipe yourself up.

49:42.354 --> 49:43.856
It's fine.

49:44.773 --> 49:47.193
You really don't listen.

50:07.588 --> 50:09.715
How are we going to wait here for hours?

50:11.717 --> 50:16.387
There's someone in Mungyeong Saejae
I can ask for help.

50:29.902 --> 50:30.903
Seonu Chan!

50:32.613 --> 50:34.907
Wow, that was fast.

50:35.699 --> 50:38.243
You little brat.

50:38.244 --> 50:40.161
You should've told me you came to Korea.

50:40.162 --> 50:42.580
You only called me now?

50:42.581 --> 50:43.665
Sorry.

50:43.666 --> 50:45.625
Oh, my.

50:45.626 --> 50:47.919
- Did you take ginseng?
- Yes.

50:47.920 --> 50:50.255
- You look so healthy.
- Right?

50:52.007 --> 50:53.217
Oh, dear.

50:53.968 --> 50:55.260
Goodness.

50:55.261 --> 50:59.055
This is Designer Song Haran,
who's working with me.

50:59.056 --> 51:00.224
Say hi.

51:00.808 --> 51:02.392
She's my grandmother.

51:02.393 --> 51:03.476
Grandmother?

51:03.477 --> 51:04.561
Hello.

51:06.313 --> 51:09.316
I haven't really made
a great first impression.

51:09.984 --> 51:11.652
- Nice to meet you.
- Hello.

51:15.489 --> 51:16.865
Let's go.

51:30.963 --> 51:34.049
- Isn't that a waste?
- You think so?

51:34.675 --> 51:38.553
But we have to empty it out a few times
to get rid of the impurities.

51:38.554 --> 51:41.181
It makes the flavor
much smoother this way.

51:42.099 --> 51:43.933
It's the same with people.

51:43.934 --> 51:47.604
We have to empty ourselves out
from time to time

51:47.605 --> 51:51.108
to clear our heads and soften our hearts.

51:52.651 --> 51:54.485
The color's nice.

51:54.486 --> 51:56.739
- Try it.
- Thank you.

51:58.407 --> 52:01.118
It's hot. Cool it down a bit.

52:02.202 --> 52:03.411
It's okay, it's not hot.

52:05.456 --> 52:06.873
You're right. It's not.

52:06.874 --> 52:09.334
How about some coffee?
I brought Mr. Park's coffee beans.

52:09.335 --> 52:11.169
I'll go and…

52:11.170 --> 52:13.714
I'd prefer tea right now.

52:18.510 --> 52:21.262
-  It's delicious.
- Right?

52:21.263 --> 52:22.264
Wow.

52:22.931 --> 52:26.267
The teapot and this cup…

52:26.268 --> 52:28.520
Everything here is so beautiful.

52:29.396 --> 52:32.608
They were all made by my grandma.

52:33.859 --> 52:34.860
She's a potter.

52:35.944 --> 52:38.363
The building outside is my studio.

52:38.364 --> 52:40.823
Would you care to take a look
once you're done?

52:46.747 --> 52:48.039
Oh…

52:48.040 --> 52:50.792
Yes… I'd love to take a look.

52:50.793 --> 52:52.211
Hey, Chaewon.

52:54.838 --> 52:56.298
What do you mean, you're sorry?

53:04.098 --> 53:05.181
What are you doing?

53:05.182 --> 53:09.227
Savoring the only meal I'm having
to get my jawline back.

53:12.856 --> 53:15.192
- Oh, my gosh.
- Samples are here!

53:18.237 --> 53:19.238
My sweet potato.

53:19.905 --> 53:23.157
I feel like
I swallowed a sock.

53:23.158 --> 53:25.868
What is it? Did something piss you off?

53:25.869 --> 53:28.371
You know the guy I was seeing?

53:28.372 --> 53:30.248
He cheated.

53:30.249 --> 53:32.709
The guy who sent the flowers?

53:32.710 --> 53:34.253
That son of a…

53:34.837 --> 53:37.256
I shouldn't swear. With who?

53:38.382 --> 53:40.884
With me. I'm the other woman.

53:41.593 --> 53:46.139
He made a ton of social media accounts
and used them to hit on girls.

53:46.140 --> 53:49.517
And I just heard
he's giving out wedding invitations.

53:49.518 --> 53:52.771
That jerk!
Should I just beat him up?

53:53.564 --> 53:56.232
Never mind. Just forget it
and pretend nothing happened.

53:56.233 --> 53:58.569
Why would I just forget about it?

54:00.696 --> 54:02.823
I'm going to crush him.

54:07.369 --> 54:13.916
♪ Happy wedding to you ♪

54:13.917 --> 54:17.211
♪ Happy wedding, dear Cha Min ♪

54:17.212 --> 54:19.047
♪ Happy wedding… ♪

54:19.882 --> 54:21.549
Ms. Song.

54:21.550 --> 54:23.927
Were you pleased
with your wedding invitations?

54:30.684 --> 54:32.019
If you found out, just go.

54:33.479 --> 54:35.021
I guess it was you.

54:35.022 --> 54:37.398
I was wondering why
some guy was picking a fight.

54:37.399 --> 54:39.567
Was he your boyfriend?

54:39.568 --> 54:40.902
What are you saying?

54:40.903 --> 54:42.862
How would you meet
a boyfriend I don't have?

54:42.863 --> 54:44.113
Boom!

54:44.114 --> 54:47.325
He threatened me with his car
and threw my phone into a mop bucket.

54:47.326 --> 54:49.828
Geez. I should've broken
both his rear-view mirrors.

54:50.704 --> 54:53.664
Tell that jerk to watch his back at night.

54:53.665 --> 54:54.832
Quit the nonsense.

54:54.833 --> 54:57.210
You should watch your back, day and night.

54:57.211 --> 54:59.462
You should sleep with one eye open.

54:59.463 --> 55:01.506
You never know when I'll crush you.

55:01.507 --> 55:03.425
Forget it. Just go.

55:04.968 --> 55:06.094
I'm not done yet.

55:14.144 --> 55:15.395
My nose…

55:16.063 --> 55:18.273
I paid a fortune for this.

55:19.149 --> 55:20.567
- Hey!
- What?

55:21.735 --> 55:23.110
You.

55:23.111 --> 55:25.072
You'd better stay out of my sight.

55:25.948 --> 55:27.491
Or I'll kick you somewhere else.

55:53.892 --> 55:55.268
Did you go somewhere?

55:55.269 --> 55:56.727
I had a meeting.

55:56.728 --> 55:58.187
Ah…

55:58.188 --> 56:01.650
But is there something wrong?
You seem pretty down.

56:02.609 --> 56:04.236
What? No.

56:05.028 --> 56:06.280
I'm fine.

56:07.072 --> 56:09.740
But why were you riding a cab?

56:09.741 --> 56:11.701
You always drive.

56:11.702 --> 56:14.662
Uh… I had to get it repaired.

56:14.663 --> 56:16.206
Ah. I see.

56:17.332 --> 56:20.168
Head inside.
I'm going to go get some coffee.

56:25.299 --> 56:27.926
I was wondering why
some guy was picking a fight.

56:29.052 --> 56:31.012
I should've broken
both his rear-view mirrors.

56:31.013 --> 56:33.514
"Cha Min." Even his name is nice.

56:33.515 --> 56:36.601
- What do you think, Mr. Yeon?
- I'm not so sure.

56:36.602 --> 56:39.604
- But, Mr. Cha…
- Ms. Kim wants you in her office.

56:40.981 --> 56:42.399
Are you…

56:43.525 --> 56:46.694
getting it repaired
because of your rear-view mirror?

56:46.695 --> 56:48.070
Yes.

56:48.071 --> 56:49.155
But why…

56:49.156 --> 56:51.575
Are you the one who met Cha Min?

56:53.410 --> 56:54.493
Uh…

56:54.494 --> 56:58.205
I have no idea what you're talking about.

56:58.206 --> 57:00.916
Oh. You really have no idea?

57:00.917 --> 57:04.504
Okay, then I'll just go meet him.

57:05.464 --> 57:08.216
Cha Min's number was…

57:10.677 --> 57:13.597
Are you going to say
"Ms. Kim is asking for you" again?

57:22.356 --> 57:25.316
Yes, Ms. Kim. I'll be there straightaway.

57:25.317 --> 57:27.027
You didn't even get a call.

57:28.362 --> 57:29.862
And she already got off work.

57:29.863 --> 57:31.447
Yes, I'm on my way.

57:31.448 --> 57:33.575
You're holding your phone upside down!

57:34.660 --> 57:36.370
Gosh, what's with him?

57:42.209 --> 57:44.670
Wait. No way…

57:48.131 --> 57:50.676
It can't be, right?

57:56.807 --> 57:57.933
Wow.

57:58.934 --> 57:59.935
Wow.

58:01.186 --> 58:04.647
Wow, they're so beautiful.

58:04.648 --> 58:07.275
Take some you like.

58:08.068 --> 58:10.487
They're not even yours. Huh?

58:11.154 --> 58:13.739
What's this drawing?

58:13.740 --> 58:15.075
- Did you draw this, too?
-  Oh…

58:15.826 --> 58:17.911
Would you like to try
making something here?

58:19.746 --> 58:21.456
The aprons…

58:38.181 --> 58:39.182
I'm done.

58:39.683 --> 58:41.893
Already?

58:42.686 --> 58:44.688
Oh, no! Wait.

58:48.734 --> 58:50.193
That was close.

58:54.990 --> 58:56.407
Let me take this call.

58:56.408 --> 58:57.451
Sure.

58:58.869 --> 58:59.953
Hello?

59:06.001 --> 59:08.544
It's so pretty.

59:08.545 --> 59:11.338
How about becoming my pupil?

59:11.339 --> 59:14.049
I mean it.

59:14.050 --> 59:16.260
Leave me your address and phone number.

59:16.261 --> 59:17.887
I'll fire it nicely and send it to you.

59:17.888 --> 59:19.556
Thank you.

59:20.432 --> 59:22.768
I guess Mr. Seonu
inherited his gift from you.

59:23.769 --> 59:27.522
That drawing was his mother's.

59:28.982 --> 59:30.649
My daughter was an artist too.

59:30.650 --> 59:33.779
Ah. So he took after his mother.

59:34.279 --> 59:38.617
He and my daughter would draw
on any piece of paper they could find.

59:42.370 --> 59:43.830
Wait here.

59:47.751 --> 59:51.671
They're pictures he drew
whenever he came here as a child.

59:54.257 --> 59:56.635
He was so excited
when he talked about work.

59:57.219 --> 59:59.054
I guess he really loved drawing.

01:00:00.388 --> 01:00:03.724
If his dad hadn't hated it so much,

01:00:03.725 --> 01:00:06.019
he would have enjoyed it much more.

01:00:08.730 --> 01:00:09.731
Ah.

01:00:10.649 --> 01:00:13.985
His father hated him doing art.

01:00:15.362 --> 01:00:17.656
But you said his mother was an artist…

01:00:19.157 --> 01:00:23.537
Her dream was to go abroad
and study more art.

01:00:24.204 --> 01:00:28.290
And Chan's father wanted her
to wait until Chan was older.

01:00:28.291 --> 01:00:29.834
Look!

01:00:29.835 --> 01:00:31.794
Why do we have
to keep arguing over this?

01:00:31.795 --> 01:00:33.087
Don't you understand?

01:00:33.088 --> 01:00:36.173
Why now? Why do you have
to go abroad to study?

01:00:36.174 --> 01:00:39.885
You know it's been my dream
since before we got married.

01:00:39.886 --> 01:00:43.222
I want to study properly
before it's too late.

01:00:43.223 --> 01:00:44.390
Fine. Do it.

01:00:44.391 --> 01:00:48.477
You can study here and think about it
again when Chan is older.

01:00:48.478 --> 01:00:50.355
You're hardly home anyway!

01:00:51.606 --> 01:00:54.316
You can stay in your lab
all you want. I'll take Chan--

01:00:54.317 --> 01:00:55.443
If you must go,

01:00:56.736 --> 01:00:58.445
then leave Chan and go by yourself.

01:00:58.446 --> 01:01:02.242
She still wanted to go so badly.

01:01:02.868 --> 01:01:06.579
So I pushed her to follow her dream

01:01:06.580 --> 01:01:09.332
and do what she wanted.

01:01:10.208 --> 01:01:14.169
She thought she had to settle down quickly
to be with Chan again,

01:01:14.170 --> 01:01:17.048
so she pushed herself too hard.

01:01:17.799 --> 01:01:19.550
And she got sick.

01:01:19.551 --> 01:01:22.679
Soon after she left the country,

01:01:23.555 --> 01:01:25.015
she...

01:01:26.600 --> 01:01:27.601
Chan!

01:01:29.269 --> 01:01:30.644
Oh, no!

01:01:30.645 --> 01:01:32.230
I can't believe what happened…

01:01:32.772 --> 01:01:35.901
He said he'd never let Chan paint again.

01:01:36.484 --> 01:01:39.446
So he sent him to America.

01:01:40.030 --> 01:01:42.657
Chan didn't get to do anything he loved,

01:01:43.283 --> 01:01:46.368
and he suffered there.

01:01:51.625 --> 01:01:53.083
KSU
KOREA SCIENCE UNIVERSITY

01:01:53.084 --> 01:01:58.924
It would've been painful
for Chan's father just to see him paint.

01:02:00.216 --> 01:02:02.509
He thinks Chan's mom left to paint...

01:02:02.510 --> 01:02:04.428
KOREAN ANIMATORS IN THE GLOBAL SPOTLIGHT

01:02:04.429 --> 01:02:07.223
...and died because of it.

01:02:09.017 --> 01:02:10.435
Okay, bye.

01:02:11.269 --> 01:02:14.521
Back then,
my daughter was all I could think about.

01:02:14.522 --> 01:02:18.360
But whenever I see Chan,
it breaks my heart.

01:02:18.818 --> 01:02:21.737
If he had his mother,

01:02:21.738 --> 01:02:25.867
at least he wouldn't have been hurt
both emotionally and physically.

01:02:26.826 --> 01:02:28.036
I've also been trapped

01:02:28.954 --> 01:02:31.206
in a long winter all by myself.

01:02:40.090 --> 01:02:41.091
Oh?

01:02:41.758 --> 01:02:42.925
Where's Ms. Song?

01:02:42.926 --> 01:02:44.427
- She's washing her hands.
- Oh.

01:02:47.389 --> 01:02:49.057
Is it just one-sided at the moment?

01:02:49.808 --> 01:02:50.809
What do you mean?

01:02:53.478 --> 01:02:55.646
Gosh, Grandma. It's not like that.

01:02:55.647 --> 01:02:57.148
Don't be silly.

01:02:57.732 --> 01:02:58.775
I can see it clearly.

01:02:59.609 --> 01:03:01.860
You have a crush on Ms. Song, don't you?

01:03:01.861 --> 01:03:03.780
It's not like that.

01:03:05.073 --> 01:03:07.324
She's someone I shouldn't like.

01:03:07.325 --> 01:03:09.452
What do you mean, someone you shouldn't…

01:03:10.036 --> 01:03:13.038
Hey.
Is she married, by any chance?

01:03:13.039 --> 01:03:14.498
No, she's not married.

01:03:14.499 --> 01:03:17.043
Then why would you say
you shouldn't like her?

01:03:17.669 --> 01:03:19.837
Ma'am, can I get a towel?

01:03:19.838 --> 01:03:21.673
Sure. Hang on.

01:03:30.807 --> 01:03:33.643
How could I like her?

01:03:35.145 --> 01:03:36.312
That would be selfish.

01:03:37.647 --> 01:03:41.233
Visit me again next time.
You can come without that chatterbox.

01:03:41.234 --> 01:03:43.736
Sure. I'll come without that chatterbox
next time.

01:03:45.196 --> 01:03:47.489
Don't build your friendship
by badmouthing me.

01:03:49.367 --> 01:03:52.077
It was so nice to meet you.

01:03:52.078 --> 01:03:54.288
- Take care.
- Stay healthy, ma'am.

01:03:56.332 --> 01:03:58.543
Um… Wait.

01:04:00.754 --> 01:04:02.337
What's that?

01:04:02.338 --> 01:04:04.674
Pardon me.

01:04:05.300 --> 01:04:06.550
This is really moisturizing.

01:04:07.927 --> 01:04:09.511
My hands are pretty rough, right?

01:04:09.512 --> 01:04:11.430
I'm always touching clay.

01:04:11.431 --> 01:04:12.931
Here, use this.

01:04:12.932 --> 01:04:17.061
I'll get pretty hands thanks to you.

01:04:17.062 --> 01:04:18.396
Let's see…

01:04:18.980 --> 01:04:22.524
You know, no matter how warm you dress,

01:04:22.525 --> 01:04:25.069
you'll catch a cold
if you don't cover your neck.

01:04:25.070 --> 01:04:27.112
- I'm okay.
- No, come here.

01:04:27.113 --> 01:04:28.907
Here.

01:04:29.824 --> 01:04:32.117
Just take it.
You ruined your scarf because of me.

01:04:32.118 --> 01:04:33.243
Hmm? Did she?

01:04:33.244 --> 01:04:35.454
Wow, look.

01:04:35.455 --> 01:04:38.123
It looks incredible on a beautiful model.

01:04:38.124 --> 01:04:39.458
Nice. This is great.

01:04:39.459 --> 01:04:41.835
Thank you. I'll use it well.

01:04:41.836 --> 01:04:43.338
Grandma.

01:04:45.632 --> 01:04:48.092
I'll come back before I go back to the US.

01:04:49.177 --> 01:04:51.221
You'd better keep your word.

01:04:52.889 --> 01:04:54.516
Chan, please. Hmm?

01:04:55.350 --> 01:04:57.018
Don't skip your meals. Okay?

01:04:57.519 --> 01:04:59.062
Of course. I eat well.

01:04:59.646 --> 01:05:01.563
You too, Grandma.

01:05:01.564 --> 01:05:03.441
-  Don't worry.
-  Okay.

01:05:05.151 --> 01:05:06.735
Bye!

01:05:06.736 --> 01:05:07.987
Drive safely!

01:05:14.285 --> 01:05:17.580
Wait. Let's check the windshield wipers
one more time.

01:05:18.164 --> 01:05:19.415
- Again?
- Yes.

01:05:23.920 --> 01:05:25.379
- Are we good?
- Wait.

01:05:29.384 --> 01:05:32.804
Okay. Done. Let's go.

01:05:36.641 --> 01:05:38.601
What? Is there something wrong again?

01:05:39.269 --> 01:05:41.062
Yes, there is.

01:05:41.688 --> 01:05:42.689
Something strange.

01:05:44.023 --> 01:05:45.483
What's strange?

01:05:48.444 --> 01:05:51.865
Why am I someone you shouldn't like?

01:05:53.616 --> 01:05:54.742
What?

01:05:56.286 --> 01:05:58.163
Why shouldn't you like me?

01:06:01.291 --> 01:06:03.793
You have a crush on Ms. Song, don't you?

01:06:04.419 --> 01:06:05.670
It's not like that.

01:06:06.254 --> 01:06:07.839
She's someone I shouldn't like.

01:06:09.090 --> 01:06:11.009
What do you mean, someone you shouldn't…

01:06:12.135 --> 01:06:15.053
Hey.
Is she married, by any chance?

01:06:15.054 --> 01:06:16.638
No, she's not married.

01:06:16.639 --> 01:06:19.266
Then why would you say
you shouldn't like her?

01:06:19.267 --> 01:06:21.518
Ma'am, can I get a towel?

01:06:21.519 --> 01:06:23.937
Sure. Hang on.

01:06:23.938 --> 01:06:26.232
I'm sorry, but I overheard.

01:06:26.858 --> 01:06:29.110
I really couldn't understand, though.

01:06:29.819 --> 01:06:32.154
You weren't saying
that you didn't like me.

01:06:32.155 --> 01:06:36.159
You said you shouldn't like me.
That sounds weird.

01:06:42.081 --> 01:06:43.624
It's not like I'm married.

01:06:43.625 --> 01:06:46.794
There's nothing between us
that would make it wrong.

01:06:47.629 --> 01:06:49.214
What did you mean by that?

01:06:53.801 --> 01:06:57.971
Oh… I'm not trying to argue or anything.
I'm just genuinely curious.

01:06:57.972 --> 01:06:59.723
Then is it okay if I like you?

01:07:41.766 --> 01:07:43.685
IN YOUR RADIANT SEASON

01:08:08.209 --> 01:08:11.670
The person
who gave me the pen died.

01:08:11.671 --> 01:08:15.507
What else was there
apart from the explosion?

01:08:15.508 --> 01:08:17.384
Honestly, I am curious.

01:08:17.385 --> 01:08:20.888
You're not telling me everything.

01:08:21.889 --> 01:08:26.394
The past might not be
as nice as you remember.

01:08:27.020 --> 01:08:29.813
I'll explain everything
if you guess it right.

01:08:29.814 --> 01:08:33.526
I feel like telling you everything today.

01:08:34.402 --> 01:08:35.445
Odd.

01:08:36.362 --> 01:08:37.488
Odd.

01:08:49.542 --> 01:08:50.625
IN YOUR RADIANT SEASON

01:08:50.626 --> 01:08:51.627
Translated by Juyoung Park
